"""Chip resistor, 2512 (6332 metric), on the Micras Altium land pattern RESC6432X89N.

The stdlib `Resistor` generic with `package="2512"` places KiCad's R_2512_6332Metric (1.225 x
3.35 mm pads); this package is the same two-terminal resistor on the land pattern of the Micras
Altium library (MicrasLib RESC6432X89N: 1.45 x 3.45 mm pads, centres 5.8 mm apart), the pads
the MicrasMainBoard current-sense shunts R31-R33 were routed and soldered on. Its configs,
properties and component type match the generic, so the board tests read its resistance the
same way.

The part comes from the instance (`mpn`, `manufacturer`, `value`, `power`): the land pattern
fits any 2512 chip resistor. The datasheet ratings of each part are cited where it is used.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Power", "Resistance", "Voltage")
load("@stdlib/utils.zen", "format_value")

value = config(Resistance)
mpn = config(str, optional=True, help="Manufacturer Part Number")
manufacturer = config(str, optional=True, help="Manufacturer")
voltage = config(Voltage, optional=True, help="Maximum operating voltage")
power = config(Power, optional=True, help="Maximum power dissipation")

properties = {
    "value": format_value(value, voltage, power),
    "package": "2512",
    "resistance": value,
}
if voltage:
    properties["voltage"] = voltage
if power:
    properties["power"] = power

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)

Component(
    name="R",
    part=Part(mpn=mpn, manufacturer=manufacturer) if mpn and manufacturer else None,
    prefix="R",
    symbol=Symbol(library="R2512.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("RESC6432X89N.kicad_mod"),
    pins={"1": P1, "2": P2},
    properties=properties,
    type="resistor",
)
